To investigate this hypothesis, we develop a suitable Riemannian metric, such that geodesic distances correspond to expected distances between one-hot encoded proteins, which are integrated along the manifold. The VAE defines a generative distribution p(X∣Z) that is governed by a neural network. Here Z is a latent variable, and X a one-hot encoded protein sequence. To define a notion of distance and shortest path we start from a curve c in latent space, and ask what is its natural length? We parametrize the curve as \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
