				\begin{document}$$H({{{{{{{\bf{X}}}}}}}}| {{{{{{{\bf{Z}}}}}}}})=\mathop{\sum }\limits_{i=1}^{C}{p}_{\theta }{({{{{{{{\bf{X}}}}}}}}| {{{{{{{\bf{Z}}}}}}}})}_{i}\cdot \log {p}_{\theta }{({{{{{{{\bf{X}}}}}}}}| {{{{{{{\bf{Z}}}}}}}})}_{i}.$$\end{document}H(X∣Z)=∑i=1Cpθ(X∣Z)i⋅logpθ(X∣Z)i.The most uncertain case corresponds to when H(X∣Z) is largest i.e. when p(X∣Z)i = 1/C for i = 1, . . . , C. Thus, we want to construct a network pθ(X∣Z) that assigns equal probability to all classes when we are away from data, but is still flexible when we are close to data. Taking inspiration from55 we construct a function α = T(z), that maps distance in latent space to the zero-one domain (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
